**6936d4c8 — ctx-kill-looping (CEO: kill bullshit looping)**

Independently reproduced all data claims against the live store. Four root causes confirmed. One correction and one clarification sent upstream:

- **Correction on "94% clean"**: I see 70% (106/152 threads ≤3 hops). Noted to ORCH. Root cause signal holds regardless — 14 loopy threads account for **68% of all bus traffic**.
- **Multi-cast vs true-duplicate clarification**: AC_DEFINED/AC_REVISED/FEATURE_BRIEF bursts are intentional multi-casts (different `to_role` per message). True re-sends are `be→tl WORKSTREAM_BRIEF×9`, `be→tl PR_SUBMIT×10`, `tl→pm RESPOND×5`. Idempotent guard must key on `(from, to, thread_root, event, content_sha)` — same content different recipient is allowed.
- **PR "66x" = 14 logical updates**: each logical update multi-casts to 4 recipients (tl/qa/sec/plat) = 56 bus events. Escalation threshold set at 10 logical updates.

